WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:02.070
- Okay. So a lot has been said recently

00:00:02.070 --> 00:00:03.660
and we don't need to rash it.

00:00:03.660 --> 00:00:06.400
I wouldn't like to, but
how, because I get it,

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:09.180
but how do you keep your
composure when so much

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:12.374
of your private life is made public?

00:00:12.374 --> 00:00:13.320
- I mean, the thing is like...

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:14.153
- It's hard.

00:00:14.153 --> 00:00:14.986
- It's hard.

00:00:14.986 --> 00:00:15.930
It's hard sometimes.

00:00:15.930 --> 00:00:16.803
And you know.

00:00:17.771 --> 00:00:19.920
But in the end of the
day, like, I'm so lucky,

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:22.770
like, I'm so lucky and
there's people dealing with so

00:00:22.770 --> 00:00:24.270
many really hard things.

00:00:24.270 --> 00:00:26.370
Like, the people of Jackson,
Mississippi don't have water.

00:00:26.370 --> 00:00:27.720
There's people everywhere dealing with

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:29.610
like, real health crises.

00:00:29.610 --> 00:00:33.600
And you know, my stuff is
out there, but I'm alive

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:36.450
and my kids are alive and
that's what gets me through.

00:00:36.450 --> 00:00:38.943
I remind myself of that every single day.

00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:41.220
- You have to so you don't get resentful.

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:42.150
- Exactly.

00:00:42.150 --> 00:00:44.070
And like I said, like
once you stop trying to

00:00:44.070 --> 00:00:46.710
control the narrative, I
mean, I'm not on the internet.

00:00:46.710 --> 00:00:48.090
I don't, I'm not on Instagram.

00:00:48.090 --> 00:00:49.410
- I don't advise it.

00:00:49.410 --> 00:00:51.150
Like, I don't do, I literally tell,

00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:52.590
especially all the young
people that come in

00:00:52.590 --> 00:00:54.690
as a young musician,
although I'm like, just like,

00:00:54.690 --> 00:00:55.710
I get that it's for work

00:00:55.710 --> 00:00:56.670
but don't live on it.

00:00:56.670 --> 00:00:58.680
That'll, it's no good for anyone.

00:00:58.680 --> 00:00:59.660
You're either gonna drink your own Koolaid

00:00:59.660 --> 00:01:01.140
and think you're amazing.

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:01.973
- Exactly.

00:01:01.973 --> 00:01:03.300
- Or you're gonna wanna
crawl in a hole and die.

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:06.180
So neither option is, is
super great for anyone.

00:01:06.180 --> 00:01:08.130
- Exactly. So I think that really helps.

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:09.480
And just, yeah, focusing on what's real,

00:01:09.480 --> 00:01:11.430
your trusted circle of friends,

00:01:11.430 --> 00:01:13.290
what's real, things that make you happy,

00:01:13.290 --> 00:01:15.180
people you love people who love you

00:01:15.180 --> 00:01:17.700
and like just stick, keeping your mind

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:18.533
on what's real.

00:01:18.533 --> 00:01:19.470
I think that's how I get through it.

00:01:19.470 --> 00:01:22.830
And also watching people, my
colleagues get through it.

00:01:22.830 --> 00:01:24.900
I mean, I think like, you're
a real great example of that.

00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:26.070
Like I said, like, you come out here

00:01:26.070 --> 00:01:27.180
and you smile and you laugh

00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:30.000
and you give joy and like,
that's inspiring to me.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.110
And I'm sure a lot of other people,

00:01:31.110 --> 00:01:32.880
who are going through hard things.

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:35.670
So that's why this is, this is important.

00:01:35.670 --> 00:01:38.130
And I think God, like, you know,

00:01:38.130 --> 00:01:39.720
it could be a lot worse

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:42.873
and we're alive and
everything's gonna be okay.

